    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-ceiling plays: **Drake Baldwin** (68.94) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Jackson Merrill** offers the most compelling upside, as the combination of a favorable matchup against Elder and a slow delivery profile from the mound significantly inflates his stolen base probability. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a premium leadoff spot and a strong xwOBA, making him a cornerstone of today's scoring projection. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.34) boasts the highest raw score, his dynamic platoon penalty against Martinez makes his matchup slightly more volatile compared to the optimized production we expect from **Jacob Wilson** (74.08), who draws a favorable 7.04 xERA target in Bratt.\n\nManagement carefully weighed the bottom of the order, ultimately opting for **Coby Mayo** (55.80) over **Curtis Mead** (53.51) for the Utility slot. While **Curtis Mead** gained significant leverage from the high-scoring park environment against Freeland, his platoon penalty as a right-handed bat against a lefty pitcher dampened his efficiency score, keeping him on the bench. We are also closely monitoring the risks associated with **Sam Antonacci** (44.04), whose score is suppressed by a brutal matchup against the elite arm of deGrom; he remains in the lineup purely for his leadoff presence and speed, but represents our highest risk for a sub-floor performance. **Andy Pages** (48.81) faces a similar hurdle against a stingy catcher and high-hold pitcher, putting his stolen base potential at risk despite a solid overall projection. Managers should keep a close eye on the weather and official lineups, as any late-breaking shifts in the order could necessitate a pivot for our lower-tier starters.",
